P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}
\] where \( n \) is the number of trials (5), \( k \) is the number of successes (2), and \( p \) is the probability of success ( \( \frac{3}{5} \)). So, we need to compute \(\binom{5}{2} \left(\frac{3}{5}\right)^2 \left(\frac{2}{5}\right)^{3}\). </think> <answer> \frac{144}{625} </answer>

